  "pythonMatchNote": "Python is not uniform. childlikeRisk, identifiabilityRisk, uniqueMarkCopyRisk and beautificationRisk are compared with an exact == \"high\"; backgroundLeakageRisk and secondaryFaceLeakageRisk go through _risk_is_high, which also accepts critical/fail/failed. The asymmetry is latent today because those four fields are produced by _risk_from_score, whose domain is low/medium/high only, so \"critical\" is unreachable from the worker. The approval gate deliberately applies the FULL vocabulary to all six: its whole premise is a document the producer did not write, and refusing a value that says \"critical\" cannot be wrong at the last authority before a face goes public. Being stricter than Python here is intentional, and tested."
